<h1>JSort</h1>
<p>
(algorithm)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
An <a href="inplacesort.html"><em>in-place sort</em></a> that partially orders the <a href="array.html"><em>array</em></a> twice with <a href="buildHeap.html"><em>build-heap</em></a>, once moving lesser items earlier and once in reverse moving greater items later, then uses <a href="insertionSort.html"><em>insertion sort</em></a> on the nearly-ordered array.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Generalization</strong> (I am a kind of ...)<br>
<a href="inplacesort.html"><em>in-place sort</em></a>.
</p>
<p>
<strong>Aggregate child</strong> (... is a part of or used in me.)<br>
<a href="buildHeap.html"><em>build-heap</em></a>, <a href="insertionSort.html"><em>insertion sort</em></a>, <a href="heap.html"><em>heap</em></a>.
</p>
<p>
<strong>See also</strong>
<a href="sort.html"><em>sort</em></a>, <a href="heapSort.html"><em>heapsort</em></a>, <a href="j_sort.html"><em>J sort</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<em>Note:
The implementation attributes the algorithm to  <a href="http://home.cc.umanitoba.ca/~morrisoj/" target="_blank">Jason Morrison</a>.</em>
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>
<h2>Implementation</h2>
Pat Morin's <a href="https://cglab.ca/~morin/misc/sortalg/" target="_blank">implementation (Java)</a>.

<hr>

